Title: GUION LARGO DE ESTRES
Credit: Generado por script
Author: fixture
Draft date: 10/02/2026

# Bloque 1

# Act One

= Introduce the world and our heroes.

EXT. CASA - DIA

Stars blanket the void. A lone satellite orbits a distant planet.

>COMMAND CENTER<

INT. CASA STATION - CONTROL ROOM - DIA

A bank of monitors flickers. JUAN VASQUEZ (40s, sharp eyes) stares at a blinking cursor.

JUAN
(whispered)
Come on, come on...

Her fingers dance across the keyboard.

STATIC
Any signal yet?

JUAN
Nothing. Six months of silence and
today's no different.

STATIC
Maybe we're looking in the wrong
frequency.

Elena leans back. Rubs her eyes.

JUAN
(pause)
Run a diagnostic on the array.

~Floating in the silence of space~

EXT. ASTEROID FIELD - NOCHE

Rocks tumble past camera. A SHIP weaves through the chaos.

The LUCIA grips the controls.

LUCIA
(bracing)
Hold on to something.

The ship lurches. Sparks fly from a console.

LUCIA
That's going to leave a mark.

CUT TO:

INT. CASA STATION - CORRIDOR - DIA

Elena walks briskly. Her footsteps echo.

She passes a NOTICE BOARD covered in faded memos.

[[Note: The notice board should have a mix of official directives and personal messages.]]

She stops at a heavy door. Punches in a code.

INT. CASA STATION - LAB - DIA

!ANA (60s, kind face, tired eyes) looks up from a microscope.

ANA
Elena. You look terrible.

JUAN
Thanks, Doc. You should see the
other guy.

They share a tired laugh.

ANA
The samples are ready.

JUAN
Good. We launch at dawn.

/*
Chapter Two notes:
- The pilot subplot resolves here
- Elena's backstory is revealed
- The alien signal is first detected
*/

SMASH CUT TO:

EXT. PLANET SURFACE - NOCHE

A barren landscape. Wind whips dust across cracked ground.

The LUCIA's ship descends through clouds.

LUCIA
(over comms)
Ground control, I have visual on
the target.

JUAN (V.O.)
Copy that. Proceed to coordinates.

The pilot lands. Steps out. Looks around.

LUCIA
(sarcastic)
Lovely vacation spot.

The pilot scans the horizon with a device.

!SCANNING THE AREA FOR ANOMALIES...

The device BEEPS. The pilot looks down.

LUCIA
What the hell is that?

A faint GLOW emanates from beneath the rocks.

EXT. PLANET SURFACE - DIA

The pilot sets up camp. A small fire crackles.

~Under the alien stars, a lone explorer wonders~

The pilot looks up. TWO MOONS hang in the purple sky.

LUCIA
(to no one)
Beautiful.

> THE END <

